Whereas the Honourable Kenneth Francis Ross, a Judge of the Superior Court of Justice in and for the Province of Ontario, will attain the age of seventy-five years on January 3, 2009, and, therefore, will cease to hold office on that date under section 99 of the Constitution Act, 1867;


 


And whereas the Honourable Kenneth Francis Ross has held judicial office for at least ten years;


 


Therefore, Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, pursuant to paragraph 42(1)(d) of the Judges Act, hereby grants an annuity of $173,333.33 to the


Honourable Kenneth Francis Ross, commencing on January 3, 2009 and continuing during his life.


 



