Whereas the Honourable Clyde K. Wells, a Judge of Appeal of the Court of Appeal of the Supreme Court of Newfoundland and Labrador, will attain the age of seventy-five years on November 9, 2012, and, therefore, will cease to hold office on that date under the provisions of subsection 99(2) of the Constitution Act, 1867;


 


And whereas the Honourable Clyde K. Wells has held judicial office for at least ten years;


 


