PC Number: 2012-1440Date: 2012-11-01


	 	 Whereas the Minister of Natural Resources and the Minister of the Environment, pursuant to subsection 9(2) of the Canada Foundation for Sustainable Development Technology Act, have consulted with the Minister of Industry; 


 


	 	 And whereas the Minister of Natural Resources and the Minister of the Environment, pursuant to subsection 9(2) of the Canada Foundation for Sustainable Development Technology Act, have proposed to appoint Jason Lee of Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island, to be a director of the Canada Foundation for Sustainable Development Technology; 


 


	 	 Therefore, His Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Natural Resources and the Minister of the Environment, pursuant to sections 9 and 10 of the Canada Foundation for Sustainable Development Technology Act, appoints Jason Lee of Charlottetown, Prince Edward Island, to be a director of the Canada Foundation for Sustainable Development Technology, to hold office during good behaviour for a term of one year, on a part-time basis.



	 	 Attendu que le ministre des Ressources naturelles et le ministre de l’Environnement ont, conformément au paragraphe 9(2) de la Loi sur la Fondation du Canada pour l’appui technologique au développement durable, consulté avec le ministre de l’Industrie; 


 


	 	 Attendu que le ministre des Ressources naturelles et le ministre de l’Environnement ont, conformément au paragraphe 9(2) de la Loi sur la Fondation du Canada pour l’appui technologique au développement durable, proposé de nommer Jason Lee, de Charlottetown (Île-du-Prince-Édouard), à titre d’administrateur de la Fondation du Canada pour l’appui technologique au développement durable, 


 


