PC Number: 2014-0331Date: 2014-03-27


Whereas by Order in Council P.C. 1999-259 of February 18, 1999, the resignation of the Honourable Mario C. DiSalle as a Judge of the Ontario Court of Justice (General Division) was accepted and he was granted an annuity of $117,200, effective March 1, 1999;


 


Whereas the Honourable Mario C. DiSalle elected under section 44.01 of the Judges Act to have the annuity to be granted to his survivor increased;


 


And whereas the Honourable Mario C. DiSalle died on January 28, 2014, leaving a survivor, Mary Anne DiSalle;


 


Therefore, His Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, pursuant to sections 44 and 44.01 of the Judges Act, grants an annuity of $67,619.39 to Mary Anne DiSalle, effective January 29, 2014, and to continue during her life.



Attendu que, en vertu du décret C.P. 1999-259 du 18 février 1999, la démission de l’honorable Mario C. DiSalle comme juge de la Cour de justice de l’Ontario (Division générale) a été acceptée et qu’il recevait une pension annuelle de 117 200 $ depuis le 1er mars 1999; 


 


Attendu que l’honorable Mario C. DiSalle a choisi, en vertu de l’article 44.01 de la Loi sur les juges, d’augmenter la pension viagère accordée à sa survivante;


 


Attendu que l’honorable Mario C. DiSalle est décédé le 28 janvier 2014 et qu’il laisse une survivante, Mary Anne DiSalle,


 


À ces causes, sur recommandation du ministre de la Justice et en vertu des articles 44 et 44.01 de la Loi sur les juges, Son Excellence le Gouverneur général en conseil accorde, à titre viager, une pension annuelle de 67 619,39 $ à Mary Anne DiSalle, payable à compter du 29 janvier 2014.

PC Number: 2014-0334Date: 2014-03-27


Whereas The Perth Chamber of Commerce has applied, pursuant to section 39 of the Boards of Trade Act, to change its name to the “Perth and District Chamber of Commerce”;


 


And whereas the Governor in Council is satisfied that the name change is not desired for any improper purpose and is not otherwise objectionable;


 


Therefore, His Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Industry, pursuant to section 39 of the Boards of Trade Act, approves the application by The Perth Chamber of Commerce to change its name to the “Perth and District Chamber of Commerce”.



Attendu que The Perth Chamber of Commerce a présenté, en vertu de l’article 39 de la Loi sur les chambres de commerce, une demande visant à faire changer sa dénomination pour « Perth and District Chamber of Commerce »;


 


Attendu que le gouverneur en conseil est convaincu que le changement de dénomination n’est pas recherché dans un but irrégulier et n’est pas autrement susceptible d’objection,


 


À ces causes, sur recommandation du ministre de l’Industrie et en vertu de l’article 39 de la Loi sur les chambres de commerce, Son Excellence le Gouverneur général en conseil approuve la demande de The Perth Chamber of Commerce visant à faire changer sa dénomination pour « Perth and District Chamber of Commerce ».

PC Number: 2014-0335Date: 2014-03-27


His Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration, pursuant to subsection 5(1) of the Department of Citizenship and Immigration Act and subsection 8(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act, approves that the Minister of Citizenship and Immigration enter into the following agreements with British Columbia, substantially in accordance with the attached draft agreements:


 


