PC Number: 2017-1302Date: 2017-10-26


Whereas the Chambre de commerce de Cowansville et région has applied, pursuant to section 39 of the Boards of Trade Act, to change its name to the “Chambre de commerce de Brome-Missisquoi”;

 

And whereas the Governor General in Council is satisfied that the name change is not desired for any improper purpose and is not otherwise objectionable;

 

Therefore, Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Industry, pursuant to section 39 of the Boards of Trade Act, approves the application by the Chambre de commerce de Cowansville et région to change its name to the “Chambre de commerce de Brome-Missisquoi”.


 

Attendu que la Chambre de commerce de Cowansville et région a présenté, en vertu de l’article 39 de la Loi sur les chambres de commerce, une demande visant à faire changer sa dénomination pour « Chambre de commerce de Brome-Missisquoi »;

 

Attendu que la gouverneure générale en conseil est convaincue que le changement de dénomination n’est pas recherché dans un but irrégulier et n’est pas autrement susceptible d’objection,

 

À ces causes, sur recommandation du ministre de l’Industrie et en vertu de l’article 39 de la Loi sur les chambres de commerce, Son Excellence la Gouverneure générale en conseil approuve la demande de la Chambre de commerce de Cowansville et région visant à faire changer sa dénomination pour « Chambre de commerce de Brome-Missisquoi ».

PC Number: 2017-1308Date: 2017-10-26


Whereas by Order in Council P.C. 2009-1554 dated September 9, 2009, the resignation of the Honourable Allen M. Linden as a Judge of the Federal Court of Appeal was accepted and he was granted an annuity of $178,133.33, effective October 7, 2009;

 

Whereas the Honourable Allen M. Linden made an election under section 44.2 of the Judges Act so that an annuity may be paid to a person to whom an annuity may not be granted under section 44 of the Judges Act;

 

And whereas the Honourable Allen M. Linden died on August 23, 2017, leaving a survivor, Joanna Linden;

 

Therefore, Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Justice, pursuant to subsection 44.2(3) of the Judges Act, grants an annuity of $46,131.84 to Joanna Linden, effective August 24, 2017, and to continue during her life.


 

Attendu qu’en vertu du décret C.P. 2009-1554 du 9 septembre 2009, la démission de l’honorable Allen M. Linden comme juge de la Cour d’appel fédérale a été acceptée et qu’il recevait une pension de 178 133,33 $ depuis le 7 octobre 2009;

 

Attendu que l’honorable Allen M. Linden a choisi, en vertu de l’article 44.2 de la Loi sur les juges, qu’une pension soit payée à une personne qui n’a pas droit à une pension viagère en vertu de l’article 44 de la Loi sur les juges;

 

Attendu que l’honorable Allen M. Linden est décédé le 23 août 2017 et qu’il laisse une survivante, Joanna Linden,

 

À ces causes, sur recommandation de la ministre de la Justice et en vertu du paragraphe 44.2(3) de la Loi sur les juges, Son Excellence la Gouverneure générale en conseil accorde une pension viagère annuelle de 46 131,84 $ à Joanna Linden, payable à compter du 24 août 2017.

PC Number: 2017-1287Date: 2017-10-26


Whereas the Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, the Honourable J. Derek Green, Chief Justice of Newfoundland and Labrador, will be unable to act from October 26 to October 30, 2017, inclusive, and from November 2 to November 3, 2017, inclusive, and it is therefore necessary that other persons be appointed Administrator for those periods;

 

Therefore, Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Canadian Heritage, pursuant to section 67 of the Constitution Act, 1867,

 

(a) terminates the appointment of the Honourable J. Derek Green as Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, effective October 26, 2017;

 

(b) appoints the Honourable B. Gale Welsh to be Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, to execute the office and functions of the Lieutenant Governor of Newfoundland and Labrador during the absence, illness or other inability of the Lieutenant Governor, effective October 26, 2017;

 

(c) terminates the appointment of the Honourable B. Gale Welsh as Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, effective October 30, 2017;  

 

(d) appoints the Honourable Raymond P. Whalen to be Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, to execute the office and functions of the Lieutenant Governor of Newfoundland and Labrador during the absence, illness or other inability of the Lieutenant Governor, effective October 30, 2017;

 

 

…/2

 


- 2 -

 

(e) terminates the appointment of the Honourable Raymond P. Whalen as Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, effective October 31, 2017;

 

(f) appoints the Honourable J. Derek Green to be Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, to execute the office and functions of the Lieutenant Governor of Newfoundland and Labrador during the absence, illness or other inability of the Lieutenant Governor, effective October 31, 2017;

 

(g) terminates the appointment of the Honourable J. Derek Green as Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, effective November 2, 2017;  

 

(h) appoints the Honourable Raymond P. Whalen to be Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, to execute the office and functions of the Lieutenant Governor of Newfoundland and Labrador during the absence, illness or other inability of the Lieutenant Governor, effective November 2, 2017;

 

(i) terminates the appointment of the Honourable Raymond P. Whalen as Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, effective November 4, 2017; and

 

(j) appoints the Honourable J. Derek Green to be Administrator of the Government of Newfoundland and Labrador, to execute the office and functions of the Lieutenant Governor of Newfoundland and Labrador during the absence, illness or other inability of the Lieutenant Governor, effective November 4, 2017.

 

 


