Whereas the Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation is a band as defined in the Indian Act;

 

Whereas in 2010, the Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation submitted to Canada the Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation Treaty 8 Agricultural Benefits Specific Claim (Specific Claim) alleging that the Crown failed to provide agricultural benefits under Treaty 8;

 

Whereas Canada, without admitting liability, accepted the Specific Claim for negotiation in 2013, pursuant to Canada’s Specific Claims Policy;

 

Whereas Canada, without admitting liability, agreed to enter into a full and final agreement with the Sturgeon Lake Cree Nation to settle the Specific Claim;

 

