Attendu que l’article 12.8.9 de l’Entente prévoit que le mandat des membres est d’une durée maximale de cinq ans et qu’il est renouvelable,

 

À ces causes, sur recommandation de la ministre des Affaires indiennes et du Nord canadien et en vertu de l’article 6 de la Loi sur le règlement de la revendication territoriale des Gwich’in ainsi que de l’alinéa 12.8.3a) et de l’article 12.8.9 de l’Entente, Son Excellence la Gouverneure générale en conseil nomme de nouveau Douglas Doan, de Yellowknife (Territoires du Nord-Ouest), membre de l’Office des ressources renouvelables des Gwich’in, pour une période de cinq ans en vigueur à la date du présent décret ou du décret du Conseil exécutif, selon la dernière de ces dates.

PC Number: 2019-1261Date: 2019-08-27


Whereas the Gwich’in Comprehensive Land Claim Agreement (“the Agreement”) was approved, given effect and declared valid by subsection 4(1) of the Gwich’in Land Claim Settlement Act; 

 

Whereas paragraph 12.8.3(a) of the Agreement provides for the joint appointment by the Governor in Council and the Executive Council of the Government of the Northwest Territories (“Executive Council”) of six members and six alternate members to the Gwich’in Renewable Resources Board; 

 

Whereas the Government of Canada has nominated Kenneth Burt Hunt of Olds, Alberta, as a member to the Gwich’in Renewable Resources Board; 

 

And whereas section 12.8.9 of the Agreement provides that each member shall be appointed for a term not to exceed five years and may be reappointed; 

 

Therefore, Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Minister of Indian Affairs and Northern Development, pursuant to section 6 of the Gwich’in Land Claims Settlement Act and paragraph 12.8.3(a) and section 12.8.9 of the Agreement, reappoints Kenneth Burt Hunt of Olds, Alberta, as a member to the Gwich’in Renewable Resources Board, for a term of five years, effective on the date of this Order in Council or the Order of the Executive Council, whichever is later.


