PC Number: 2019-1367Date: 2019-11-20


Her Excellency the Governor General in Council, on the recommendation of the Prime Minister, pursuant to the definition Designated Minister in section 2 of the Business Development Bank of Canada Act, and pursuant to paragraph (d) of the definition appropriate Minister in section 2 of the Financial Administration Act and subparagraph (a)(ii) of the definition appropriate Minister in subsection 83(1) of the Financial Administration Act,  

 

(a) repeals Order in Council P.C. 2018-1020 of July 18, 2018;

 

(b) designates the Minister for International Trade, a member of the Queen's Privy Council for Canada, as the Designated Minister for the purposes of the Business Development Bank of Canada Act; and  

 

(c) designates the Minister for International Trade, a member of the Queen's Privy Council for Canada, as the appropriate Minister with respect to the Business Development Bank of Canada for the purposes of the Financial Administration Act.

 


 

