Whereas the Canadian Judicial Council has nominated the Honourable Louise Charron, C.C., to be a member of the Independent Advisory Board for Supreme Court of Canada Judicial Appointments; 

 

Therefore, His Excellency the Administrator of the Government of Canada in Council, on the recommendation of the Prime Minister, pursuant to paragraph 127.1(1)(c) of the Public Service Employment Act and Order in Council P.C. 2016-693 of July 29, 2016, appoints the Honourable Louise Charron, C.C., of Ottawa, Ontario, to be a special adviser to the Prime Minister, to serve as a member of the Independent Advisory Board for Supreme Court of Canada Judicial Appointments, to hold office during pleasure for a term of one year.


